Z||000000||phillip||05-21-2000||07:03 PM||||<BR>i think i am about to try a head gasket change. but, if i have the head off should i automaticaly take the head to have it worked on since it is off. is there any way of telling that this is nessesary using a "shade tree"method.<P>this is for the indy i just got. i was told the head gasket needed changing. hope i don't find any thing more serious. it runs rough and smells real "carbony". ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-21-2000||11:41 PM||||If your taking the head off might as well call around a see what they charge to clean it up and replace seals. I did my V-6's and they charged me $75.00 per head. (I had the other parts they just cleaned and installed the new parts.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||05-22-2000||02:25 PM||||If the only source for "it needs a head gasket" is the person you bought it from I would do some diagnostics before jumping into the engine. Of the cars I've seen that "needed a head gasket" they have actually needed anything from a tune up to a new engine (a couple actually needed a head gasket   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).<P>I would check things like spark plugs, distributor, sensors, ECM codes, etc. before tearing it down. <P>If you do take the head off, the $75 to $100 to have a machine shop check out and refurbish a head is money well spent.<P>Added: There are too many things that can cause problems that can go unnoticed without precision tools to risk re-doing all that work.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 05-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fastonpumpgas||05-23-2000||11:07 PM||||i dont know if you want top get into geting new heads , but they made a small and a large valve head for fiero (HO). i pocket ported mine, dont mess with the vein.   maybe do some exhaust manifold grinding while you have them off..  i think that is a big problem with fieros....  Good luck.. never go cheap.. you will always regret it||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero mistress||05-24-2000||12:33 AM||||On my 84 SE, we picked it up in March, it ran like crap, wouldn't even pull it's own weight.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Well, we replaced all the usual parts and when we were starting to consider replacing the head, we decided to try checking the timing (a suggestion from this forum), whoa!! it made all the diference in the world!  Runs like a champ, now!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I would check the timing FIRST!  We even purchased it from a mechanic.  And there is a special way of setting the timing, you have to trip the computer before starting the engine so you can set the base timing.  (We are having soooo much fun learning to work on our Fieros...)<P>Hope this helps.<P>Mistress||||reg||1
